Subject: [PATCH 006/260] [ae-patch] Open a plan limits popover from the
 composer's context ring

Clicking the context ring shows the Claude Code and Codex subscription
windows (percent used, reset times, when each reading was taken) from
omnigent-ae's GET /v1/ae/limits. The component is the new
web/src/components/AePlanLimits.tsx; ChatPage.tsx gains the import and
mounts it beside the ring, which stays as upstream renders it. Since v0.15.0
the ring is ComposerContextRing in the composer's workspace bar, itself a
button in a row whose layout upstream's tests pin, so the popover adds no
element: it anchors to the ring a click lands on.

